    public const FAMILY_INSTRUCTIONS = <<<'MARKDOWN'
This process serves one Git family and starts without a selected code root. First call repository-context action=bind with the absolute task workspace. It must identify exactly one member of this family. Once bound, the process stays on that code root; use another process for another worktree. repository-context action=status reports current rule origin, profile, fingerprint and effective permissions. Before binding only discovery metadata and repository-context are available. Then call the tool needed for the requested work. Binding and refreshing do not prepare a map, begin a task or run an audit. Task beginning/check and audits are optional actions for work that asks for them. Use architecture-map prepare only when a map is wanted. If a tool cannot answer, continue ordinary source search and report the gap. Settings refresh on the next request; stale results and comparisons never PASS. Preserve an existing task beginning through settings changes and resume. Basic and advisory are defaults; settings do not grant Enforce, Deep, execution, runtime or writes. Record Deep consent only after explicit human approval for this code root and task. Explicit execution/runtime/write permissions are separate. Read freshness, uncertainty and analysis completeness. Source relationships and candidate tests prove no execution, coverage or passing tests.
MARKDOWN;

    public const GRAPH_WORKFLOW = <<<'MARKDOWN'
Basic: architecture-map prepare; keep job_id while building, search sources, collect with result. Status/pending never proves timing. runtime_semantics=2 confirms product/scope/epoch/snapshot/session. last_confirmed confirms an observed prefix, not content now; stale has pending changes; unverified gives a reason; current requires full content pre/post. Legacy fresh is null for last_confirmed/unverified. Read checks_complete, diagnostics/limits, cache read/write, execution and deadlines separately. On restart_required restart MCP. No daemon/autostart. User/code renews idle 900 s; global pressure permits earlier LRU. Find name/path/route/table/kind via architecture-search; use its ID in architecture-graph. context: one hop; path: target; impact: dependents/test candidates. Links/tests prove no execution, coverage or PASS. posting_budget uses exact dictionary fallback. limit=0 summarizes; follow next/snapshot; stale_snapshot restarts offset=0; cursor is no lease. Target only for path. Legacy search/path/reach and impact delete/move/signature remain. no_path_in_analyzed_graph is source-only; inspect unresolved sources.
MARKDOWN;

    public const RESULT_INTERPRETATION = <<<'MARKDOWN'
Basic/advisory default. Read analysis.mode/checks_complete/deep_run and control.blocking; exit 0 is not PASS. Strict evaluates warnings, full expands output, enforce blocks. If Deep is needed, ask a concrete consent question first. After approval record analysis-consent per repo/task and use analysis_mode=deep/task or --mode=deep/--task. Runtime/custom PHP need separate permission; refusal leaves Basic available. For important gaps read source and cite the file/relationship or uncertainty. If missing information prevents a correct choice, ask one concrete question; listing gaps is insufficient. Try to fix new errors; hand off failures/unverified checks. Candidate tests are not coverage or PASS. Use explain-finding and doctor. Report tests actually run.
MARKDOWN;

    public const SERVER_INSTRUCTIONS = <<<'MARKDOWN'
Basic source analysis and advisory reaction are the defaults, including old profiles. Read analysis.mode/checks_complete/deep_run and control.blocking. A successful process exit is not PASS. Strict changes warning evaluation; only enforce enables blocking. Full only expands presentation. When Deep is needed, first ask a concrete consent question. Only after approval record analysis-consent for this repository/task, then supply analysis_mode=deep and task. Refusal leaves Basic tools available. Deep grants neither runtime nor custom PHP. For important gaps search and read source, cite the file and relationship or explain uncertainty; ask one concrete question when missing information prevents a correct change; listing gaps alone is insufficient. Try to repair new errors; hand off remaining failures and unverified checks.


Before deleting, moving or changing a method signature, call impact with the intended change and concrete signature or target_class/target_path when known. Include demonstrated follow-up edits in the authorized task and inspect unresolved source before dependent decisions. An impact finding does not require another approval for work already authorized. For a known ordinary edit use architecture-context. Inspect incoming/outgoing execution directions; caller siblings and shared tables never connect processes. For immutable proposal pages use impact page=1, then pagination.next report_id/page/limit without subject or proposal. Restart after changed source metadata; dispatch and candidate tests do not prove execution or PASS.
When .architecture-kit/target.json exists, read its declaration with file-rules. Full architecture-target and guard target=true require prior human consent and analysis_mode=deep/task. Read current/expected facts, migration order, suppression labels, uncertainty and freshness. Target declarations never change current audit; guard includes the target only with target=true. Never write, approve or refresh a reference candidate automatically.

Use classification from file-rules, architecture-context, search and impact as the shared source for declared roles, application kinds and module ownership. PHP kind is separate. Read provenance; declarations do not prove compliance or enable profiles. Declared roles and kinds override default placement conventions below. Respect existing directories. During a related change, you may propose a named module with Actions and Queries subdirectories, but list the affected files, reasons, uncertainties, references and registration changes, and test consequences. Keep this proposal separate from accepted project declarations. Require user approval before moving files or editing declarations. Keep models in app/Models by default; shared models may remain unassigned. Respect models already inside modules. Never scaffold or reorganize modules as an unrelated cleanup.

For package contract changes, use MCP public-api or architecture-kit:public-api with a Git before revision. Read partial/freshness/check rows and explicit 0.x policy; this does not approve or publish a release. Architecture Kit is mandatory for this Laravel project. config/architectures.php is the source of truth. Before coding, your first Architecture Kit MCP call MUST be enabled-architectures. Use it to identify enabled patterns and relevant architecture-kit-* skills. If only a name/path fragment, route or command name is known, call search and choose a candidate explicitly. Inspect selector_scope and notes before passing its selector to impact/path. Search does not prove runtime registration or execution. Before changing an existing project symbol, call architecture-context with its exact FQCN or app-relative path and inspect the returned dependencies, dependents, violations, and files. Inspect execution.authorization in impact for precise Gate/policy rules, route and Form Request checks, conditions, boolean/exception usage, shared rule site counts and unresolved boundaries. Use path to expand individual authorization chains and reach for immutable continuation pages. Inline allowIf/denyIf bypass policies and hooks; missing checks are not security verdicts. Use reach for unique direct and exclusively indirect reach counts and continuation pages of one immutable report. Keep code, entrypoints and DATA units separate; inspect lower bounds and freshness. Source changes require a new report. Before changing a class, file or method, also call impact. Inspect resolved chains, possible contract calls, callable references and class-only context separately. Resolve uncertainty before dependent decisions. Inspect execution.routes for HTTP declarations and their precise handler-to-symbol chains, plus execution.unresolved, status and freshness. Route declarations do not prove active runtime routes. Sources are discovered automatically without booting the application. Test candidates are not coverage or PASS. A relationship is not a BREAKING verdict. Before relocating a PHP file or renaming a class/namespace, use impact with change=move and optional target_class/target_path. Inspect Composer mappings, namespace dependencies and uncertain registrations; no source is rewritten. Before removing a method, class or PHP file, use impact with change=delete. Before changing a method declaration, use change=signature and the proposed signature. Inspect breaking rows and check rows; no breaking rows does not prove safety. Ask the user before expanding the agreed change scope. Do not implement architecture-sensitive code before this preflight. Before upgrading a package, call plan-upgrade and load only its active atomic upgrade skill. For full architecture details, call the architecture-rules tool or read the architecture-kit://guideline resource. After code changes, call guard before final response. If generated resources are stale, rerun php artisan architecture-kit:install; do not edit generated Architecture Kit files manually.

Before coding, call MCP `enabled-architectures` first. Use it to identify enabled patterns and relevant `architecture-kit-*` skills.
